file at the root of this repository.

Termixgo reuses Termigo's design vocabulary and behavioural conventions, and
reimplements them in Go for a terminal-only runtime. No source file from the
original TypeScript or Rust codebases is copied verbatim; the shared parts are
protocol shapes, tool semantics, prompt structure and file layout.

Files whose behaviour is intentionally aligned with the original, so that the
two stay compatible:

  internal/config       state layout and folder trust
  internal/agent        tool semantics and the agent loop
  internal/provider     BYOK provider registry and wire formats
  internal/skill        SKILL.md discovery and frontmatter
  internal/telegram     companion bot commands and pairing

Third-party Go modules retain their own licences; see go.sum for the exact
versions in use.
